{**
 * c-icon - a small drawing beside a word, or standing in for one.
 *
 * Drawn in the ink of the text around it (currentColor) and at a size read out
 * of --icon-size, so a theme recolours and resizes every icon at once and none
 * of them carries a colour or a length of its own.
 *
 * Beside a word that already says what it means, an icon is decoration and is
 * hidden from assistive technology; given a label, it stands on its own and is
 * announced as an image under that name. There is no third case - an icon a
 * screen reader announces as nothing in particular.
 *
 * Which icons there are is Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Icon, and a
 * name that is not one of its cases stops the page rather than leaving an empty
 * place in it.
 *}

{define icon, string $name, ?string $label = null}
    {var Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Icon $icon = Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\Icon::from($name)}

    <svg
        class="c-icon"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        focusable="false"
        n:attr="role: $label === null ? null : 'img', aria-label: $label, aria-hidden: $label === null ? 'true' : null"
    >
        {switch $icon->value}
            {case 'sign-out'}
                <path d="M10 4H6a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v14a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h4" />
                <path d="M15 8l4 4-4 4" />
                <path d="M19 12H10" />
            {case 'chevron-down'}
                <path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6" />
            {case 'close'}
                <path d="M6 6l12 12" />
                <path d="M18 6L6 18" />
        {/switch}
    </svg>
{/define}
